 "unhandled_root_fields": {
  "description": "BOG GUARDIAN (bog_guardian.bbmodel)  -  notes\n============================================================\nScale 1 unit = 2.8125 cm. Origin between the feet at y=0, faces -Z, creature right = +X.\n\nSIZE\n  Cubes: 52 (budget 60), 1 texture 256x256 embedded (bog_guardian.png), 1 texel per unit.\n  Rest/model geometry: top of head y=107 (3.01 m); horn tip y=121 (3.40 m total).\n  In the idle stance (hunched, head low and forward): top of head y=100.9 (2.84 m), horn tip y=114.7 (3.23 m).\n  Idle body extents (club and pond weed excluded, all idle frames): x -40.7..39.8, y 0..117.8, z -38.6..14.2.\n\nHIT BOX (W x H x D, units; centred on x=0)\n  Main body: 81 x 118 x 53, spanning z -39..14 (= 2.29 x 3.31 x 1.48 m). One box is enough; the club is not part of the hit box.\n  (Height includes the horn; without the horn the body box is 102 high.)\n  Death (final lying pose): body covers x -70..67, y 0..35, z -119..7 -> corpse box 137 x 35 x 126.\n  Overhead smash impact point (club head centre at key time): x 9, y 7, z -76  -> about 2.1 m in front of the origin.\n\nMOVE SPEEDS (in-place cycles, stride matched to speed; verified by ground-contact speed of planted feet)\n  walk: 32.0 units/s = 0.90 m/s, cycle 1.6 s, stride (one full cycle) 51.2 units = 1.44 m\n  run : 85.3 units/s = 2.40 m/s, cycle 0.8 s, stride 68.3 units = 1.92 m (heavy jog; club lifted off the ground)\n\nCLIPS (name, length, loop mode, events)\n  idle             3.600 s  loop  breathing, sway, head turn to its left ~1.4 s, two sniffs ~2.5 s; club head resting on ground behind\n  walk             1.600 s  loop  club dragged behind, head of club stays on y=0; 2 steps per cycle\n  run              0.800 s  loop  club carried trailing, lifted\n  attack_overhead  2.600 s  once  KEY (impact) = 1.30 s. wind-up 0-0.75 s, hang 1.05-1.15 s, smash 1.15-1.30 s, two hands on the club ~0.6-1.6 s, recover to idle by 2.6 s\n  alarmed          4.750 s  once  drops club 0.208 s (falls, settles flat on y=0 by ~0.71 s, world-fixed while on the ground), arms up and shaking 0.65-2.2 s, roar 0.65-2.2 s, stomps (impacts) at 1.25 s (right foot) and 1.875 s (left foot), grabs club 3.00 s, drags it back into the idle pose\n  injured          0.625 s  once  hit from the front, peak recoil 0.07 s, back to idle pose at the end\n  death            2.750 s  hold  hit 0.1 s, drops club 0.125 s, staggers back, knees buckle ~1.15 s, falls forward, body lands 1.875 s, settles, holds last frame. Lying body rests exactly on y=0 (lowest point 0.00). Falls forward along -Z (head ends ~3.1 m in front of the origin).\n  roar             2.000 s  once  optional extra: crouch, rears up and roars 0.75-1.4 s, arms spread; club stays in hand\n  Key times are also keyframed on the root bone (a rotation key at the exact time) and stored as animation\n  markers (attack: 1.30; alarmed: 0.208 release, 1.25/1.875 stomps, 3.0 grab; death: 0.125 release, 1.875 land).\n  Blockbench keyframes have no name field, so the root key is unnamed; the times above are authoritative.\n\nATTACHMENT POINTS (empty groups, pivot in rest pose)\n  slot_head        parent head         pivot (0, 107, -16)\n  slot_back        parent torso        pivot (0, 80, 13)\n  slot_quiver      parent torso        pivot (7, 86, 12)\n  slot_shoulder_r  parent torso        pivot (26, 92, -1)\n  slot_carry       parent torso        pivot (0, 66, -18)\n  slot_hand_r      parent hand_r       pivot (26.0, 30.0, -1.0)\n  slot_shield_l    parent arm_lower_l  pivot (-34, 50, -1)\n  slot_hand_l      parent hand_l       pivot (-26, 30, -1)\n  slot_hip_r       parent hips         pivot (18, 47, 5)\n  slot_hip_l       parent hips         pivot (-18, 47, 5)\n\nCLUB (bone \"club\" under slot_hand_r, pivot = grip = slot_hand_r pivot)\n  Knotted hardwood club, 7 cubes. Length 53 units (1.49 m): pommel end +7, head end -46 along its local Z.\n  Grip at the item origin, handle runs toward -Z (head at local z -34..-46).\n  Rest/default pose: the club group carries a rest rotation (-33.54, -172, 0) so it trails behind with the head\n  on the ground (y=0) while the arm hangs. In clips the club rotation/position are keyed densely.\n  Second grip (two-handed attack): 13 units (0.37 m) along the handle from the grip,\n  toward the club head (local 0,0,-13 relative to the grip). The left hand is IK-placed there in attack_overhead.\n\nSKELETON\n  Baseline names: root > hips > torso > head (> jaw, slot_head); arm_upper/arm_lower/hand _r/_l;\n  leg_upper/leg_lower/foot _r/_l; slots as listed. Extra bones: jaw, club, weed_* (pond-weed strands,\n  simulated secondary motion, safe for the game to ignore). No glow_* parts (not glowing).\n\nCONVENTIONS / CAVEATS\n  - Rotation signs follow the reference files (example_1/example_2), which use Bedrock-style signs\n    (X and Y animation rotations negated relative to raw Blockbench preview). If the game plays the\n    references correctly it will play this file correctly.\n  - Loco cycles are in place; the death clip moves the body forward (root position) as it falls.\n  - Pond weed and club drops are simple simulations baked to keys (24 fps legs/club, 12 fps weed).\n"
 },
 "resolution": {
  "width": 256,
  "height": 256
 },
